#DESCRIPTION
Explicit full PIC (kinetic ions AND kinetic electrons, leapfrog) parallel
whistler wave test. Same geometry, normalization and seed as the semi-implicit
full-PIC variant (PARAM.in), but with m_i/m_e = 25 and warmer electrons so the
explicit solver is stable and resolves the Debye length: in code units
c = 1, d_i ~ v_A ~ Omega_i ~ 1, omega_pe = 5, v_te = 0.3 (T_e = 4361 K),
lambda_De = 0.06 = 0.6 dx, omega_pe dt = 0.1, c dt/dx = 0.2. The n = 1 mode
(k d_i = 0.982) must follow the full cold-plasma R-mode for m_i/m_e = 25.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 6.4 d_i]
 3.2                    xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#FIELDSOLVER
explicit

#FIELDINTEGRATOR
leapfrog                fieldIntegrator

#FIELDSUBCYCLE
1                       nSubcycle
F                       isAutoSubcycle

Two kinetic species: ions (q = 1, m = 1) and electrons (q = -1, m = 1/25).
#PLASMA
2                       nS
1.0                     mass        Species 0: ions
1.0                     charge
1.0/25.0                mass        Species 1: electrons
-1.0                    charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]       ions, v_ti = 0.09 c
5.0                     rho [/cc]   Species 1: electrons (n_e = n_i = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
4361.0                  T [K]       electrons, v_te = 0.3 c
1.0439e-8               bx [T]      uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

Same transverse circularly-polarized right-hand seed (frac = 0.02) and Alfven
velocity kick as the hybrid variant, applied to both species.
#TESTCASE
HybridWave

#WAVEIC
T                       rightHand      right-hand (whistler) helicity
1                       waveMode       box-fundamental (n=1) mode

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
250                     nParticle per cell in X
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
10                      dn
-1                      dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
24.0                    TimeMax   ~3 full-EM whistler periods (T = 8.0 s here)
